-- statement:
--   A tracial vector for a von Neumann algebra M on a complex Hilbert space H is a unit vector (the vacuum) that is tracial on M, meaning ⟨Ω, AB Ω⟩ = ⟨Ω, BA Ω⟩ for all A, B in M, and separating, meaning A Ω = 0 forces A = 0 for A in M. It gives the trace τ(A) = ⟨Ω, AΩ⟩ and word moments τ(X_{i1}⋯X_{ik}) of an n-tuple X of operators. FreeSubalgebras τ says a family of subalgebras is free: any product of centered elements (trace zero) drawn from the subalgebras, with consecutive indices different, has trace zero. FreeStandardNoise τ X S says each S_i has moments τ(S_i^k) equal to the Catalan number C_{k/2} for even k and 0 for odd k (semicircular), and the algebra generated by X and the algebras generated by the individual S_i are free. The polynomial L² space is the closure of the span of the vectors w(X)Ω over all words w. The derivative moment of word w in direction i sums, over positions where w has letter i, the product of the moment of the prefix and the moment of the suffix. A conjugate system is a tuple ξ of vectors in that L² space with ⟨ξ_i, w(X)Ω⟩ equal to this derivative moment for every word. The free Fisher information is the infimum of Σ‖ξ_i‖² over conjugate systems, valued in [0,∞]. The heat tuple is X_i + √s S_i. The quantity chiStar is (n/2)·log(2πe) plus half the integral over s>0 of the positive part of n/(1+s) minus the Fisher information of the heat tuple, minus half the integral of the opposite positive part, as an extended real. For microstates, Hermitian d×d matrices are parametrized by real coordinates in Euclidean space (diagonal entries and real and imaginary off-diagonal parts scaled by 1/√2), with operator norm and normalized-trace matrix moments. The microstate set for radius R, word length m, size d and tolerance ε contains tuples with all operator norms at most R and all moments of words of length at most m within ε of the corresponding moments of X. chiCutoff is the infimum over m and ε>0 of the limsup in d of d⁻² log Lebesgue volume of microstates plus (n/2) log d, and chi is the supremum of chiCutoff over R>0, the microstate free entropy.
